-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Olli & Lissa III: The Candlelight Adventure
  Publisher   Codemasters, 1989
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch
  (one of these files):

  File        Olli & Lissa III - The Candlelight Adventure
              (1989)(Codemasters).tzx
  MD5         e18af253f5178fb1cb9df1e313a2d856

  File        Olli & Lissa III - The Candlelight Adventure
              (1989)(Codemasters).tap
  MD5         d720d69bed26c6341fb0cf3307c9fefd

  File        Olli & Lissa III - The Candlelight Adventure
              (1989)(Codemasters)[a].tzx
  MD5         8bb4c68835bb81ae109c64a112fa334b

  File        Olli & Lissa III - The Candlelight Adventure
              (1989)(Codemasters)[a2].tzx
  MD5         50191f8f29336f94c5f6f0ea564e9c06

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    All 66 figures of the first rooms painted: Olli green, the
              creatures in their own colours. A first pass. Off by default. A
              painted set, colourist not named.

  Pace        original

  Note        Olli and the creatures are hardware sprites laid on their own
              pixels, so they no longer take the colours of the room they
              cross; the game underneath is unchanged. Default: the figures in
              white, Olli with a black edge. Enhanced paints them. The pick-
              ups and the panel do not move and stay as the game draws them.
              Proven on two machine-played recordings of the first seven
              rooms; a figure the patch does not know is left as the game
              draws it.

